{"id":"gen-1792326388-ePrZMCKQV1cxXGrxkDGO","object":"chat.completion","created":1792326388,"model":"cohere/north-mini-code:free","provider":"Cohere","system_fingerprint":null,"service_tier":null,"choices":[{"index":0,"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop","native_finish_reason":"complete","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"R-b Verdikt: A — Begründung: Das Hinzufügen von Parser-Armen für ellipsoid und normal_gravity liefert die fehlenden skalaren Referenzkonstanten und ermöglicht so die Registrierung von a, 1/f, GM, omega, gamma0 usw. Dies folgt dem bewährten Muster, das von River und Mountain verwendet wird, und hält die Änderungen konsistent. Ohne diese Arme bleibt N = T/gamma0 None, was die GRS80/gamma0-Registrierung unbrauchbar macht. — Riss: N bleibt None (ungemessene gamma0) und calc.js bleibt lokal-only, sodass die Registrierung nicht vollständig populliert werden kann.\n\nR-f Verdikt: A — Begründung: D=2190 (XGM2019e_2159) ist das offizielle Teilmodell, bleibt unter der 2 GiB-Freigabegrenze und vermeidet den 5,95 GiB großen Full-Dump, der nicht freigegeben werden kann. Es reduziert den Speicherbedarf und den Streaming-Overhead, während es die wesentlichen Modell-Daten beibehält. Die Epoche ist im Datensatz nicht verankert, was den Compiler dazu zwingt, ohne --epoch abzulehnen, sodass ein separater Epochen-Handling-Schritt erforderlich ist, bevor der Block verwendet werden kann. — Riss: Die Epoche ist im Datensatz nicht verankert, der Compiler verweigert den Build ohne --epoch, und die Diskrepanz zwischen Abstract (5399) und Datei (5480) schafft Unsicherheit.\n\nR-g Verdikt: B — Begründung: Die Behebung des kg/(m^2 s)-Token-Parsers und die Einführung einer Achse für Stern-Metadaten beheben die kritischsten Parsing-Probleme und stellen die Nutzbarkeit für den Großteil der Restgruppen wieder her. Dieser minimale Ansatz vermeidet das enorme architektonische Risiko, alle Arme zu erstellen, und liefert dennoch funktionale Daten. Das Ignorieren der anderen fünf Restgruppen (eionet_cdr, Infraschall, Feuerstrahlung, TEC/Pseudoranges/Delay, vis_nmi/morph_sigma, FDSN BHZ-Identität) lässt sie weiterhin defekt und könnte zu nachgelagerten Fehlern führen. — Riss: Sechs Restgruppen haben immer noch keine Quantity-/Channel-Arme (z. B. FDSN BHZ-Identität), sodass das System trotz der Parser-Fixes unvollständig bleibt.","refusal":null,"reasoning":"We need to answer three questions, each in format:\n\n`R-<x> Verdikt: <A|B|C|D> — Begründung: <two sentences> — Riss: <strongest counter-evidence or unmeasured size>`\n\nWe need to choose one of the options for each. Provide a verdict (A/B/C/D) and a brief justification (two sentences) and a \"Riss\" (counter-evidence or unmeasured size) field.\n\nWe must not invent facts. Use given info. Let's analyze each.\n\n### R-b: GRS80/gamma0 registry\n\nProblem: phi/sources.phi missing arm for scalar reference constants; a, 1/f, GM, omega, gamma_e, gamma_p measured but not registerable. N = T/gamma0 in src/archivar/gfc.rs:404 remains None. calc.js is local-only (no license notice); GeographicLib is MIT code, not dataset.\n\nOptions:\nA new directives ellipsoid + normal_gravity (parser arm in src/archivar/parse.rs; River builds, Mountain sets).\nB own constants/reference block with url/terms (url/terms for calc.js not occupied).\nC local-only, N remains pending.\nD only future gfc block, a/f/omega/gamma0 remain unregistered.\n\nAdditional: Does N remain pending — as pending line or as absence?\n\nWe need to decide which is best. The issue is missing arm for scalar reference constants. Options A adds directives for ellipsoid and normal_gravity, which would provide those constants. B creates own constants block with url/terms, but calc.js not occupied. C leaves local-only, N pending. D only future gfc block, leaving constants unregistered.\n\nProbably best is A: add parser arm for ellipsoid + normal_gravity, because it directly addresses missing scalar reference constants. It uses existing parser arm pattern (River builds, Mountain sets). So verdict A.\n\nJustification: two sentences. Riss: strongest counter-evidence or unmeasured size. Counter-evidence: N = T/gamma0 remains None because gamma0 not registered; also calc.js local-only no license. So Riss could be \"N remains None (unmeasured size)\". Or \"Missing parser arm for scalar reference constants\". Provide something.\n\n### R-f: gfc block\n\nProblem: Model/Cap, epoch, ttl and bootstrap order not settable; 5399 (abstract) vs 5540/5480 (file). Sizes: D=5540 5.95 GiB (not release-worthy), D=3211 2.146 GB (891 kB under 2 GiB), D=2190 999 MB, D=760 121 MB, Cap 719 108 MB. No streaming (peak 8-21 GB). Epoch nowhere occupied; compiler refuses without --epoch. File tail: non-zero up to m=5480; paper says 5480; abstract 5399.\n\nOptions:\nA D=2190 (XGM2019e_2159, official partial model).\nB Cap 3211.\nC full D=5540 (split/R2).\nD D=760 or Cap 719.\n\nAdditional: epoch — search full-text evidence, static compiler path build, or no block set? ttl NO_CADENCE=33554432 s?\n\nWe need to choose best. The official partial model D=2190 is 999 MB, fits under 2 GiB, and is release-worthy. It also likely has epoch defined? Not sure. The abstract says 5399 but file says 5480; epoch not occupied. However, the compiler refuses without --epoch, so we need epoch set. If we choose D=2190, we still need epoch. But maybe we can set epoch via static compiler path? The question asks to choose one option. Probably A is best because it's the official partial model, smaller, release-worthy. The other options are larger or not official. So verdict A.\n\nJustification: two sentences. Riss: counter-evidence: epoch not set, compiler refuses; also abstract vs file discrepancy. So Riss could be \"epoch not occupied, compiler error\". Or \"size 2190 MB still > 2 GiB? Actually 999 MB < 2 GiB, okay.\n\n### R-g: P10 residuals\n\nProblem: six residual groups have name and unit but no matching Quantity-/Channel-Arm: eionet_cdr_* (276, kg, tau=1a), Infrasound signal sizes, Fire radiation power/bandpowers, TEC/Pseudoranges/Delay, vis_nmi/morph_sigma, Stellar metadata (Teff/logg/mag), FDSN BHZ channel identity, kg/(m^2 s)-token (parser splits on whitespace).\n\nOptions:\nA build all arms (largest architectural act).\nB smallest safe subset (kg/(m^2 s)-parser fix + stellar metadata axis).\nC build nothing, let cracks fall.\nD one form per residual.\n\nAdditional: Does parser fix + stellar axis suffice, or is FDSN key splitting also minimally needed?\n\nWe need to decide. The smallest safe subset likely B, focusing on parser fix for kg/(m^2 s) token and stellar metadata axis. That addresses the most critical parsing issue. The other groups are less essential. So verdict B.\n\nJustification: two sentences. Riss: strongest counter-evidence: missing FDSN BHZ channel identity and other residual groups still broken, leading to incomplete coverage. Or \"six residual groups still lack Quantity-/Channel-Arms\". Provide that.\n\nNow format each answer:\n\n`R-b Verdikt: A — Begründung: ... — Riss: ...`\n\nMake sure exactly format: `R-<x> Verdikt: <A|B|C|D> — Begründung: <two sentences> — Riss: <strongest counter-evidence or unmeasured size>`\n\nWe need three separate answers, each with its own R-x. Probably each on separate lines.\n\nLet's craft.\n\nR-b: Verdict A. Begründung: two sentences: \"Adding parser arms for ellipsoid and normal_gravity provides the missing scalar reference constants, enabling registration of a, 1/f, GM, omega, gamma0, etc. This follows the existing pattern used by River and Mountain builds, keeping changes consistent.\" Second sentence: \"Without these arms, N = T/gamma0 stays None, preventing the GRS80/gamma0 registry from being usable.\" Riss: \"N remains None (unmeasured gamma0) and calc.js stays local‑only, so the registry cannot be fully populated.\"\n\nR-f: Verdict A. Begründung: two sentences: \"D=2190 (XGM2019e_2159) is the official partial model, fits under the 2 GiB release threshold, and avoids the 5.95 GiB full dump that is not release‑worthy. It also reduces storage and streaming overhead while preserving the core model data.\" Second: \"The epoch is still missing, causing the compiler to reject builds without --epoch, so a separate epoch handling step is required before the block can be used.\" Riss: \"Epoch not occupied in the file, compiler error without --epoch, and abstract/file size mismatch (5399 vs 5480) create uncertainty.\"\n\nR-g: Verdict B. Begründung: two sentences: \"Fixing the kg/(m^2 s) token parser and adding a stellar metadata axis resolves the most critical parsing failures and restores usability for the majority of residual groups. This minimal change avoids the massive architectural effort of building all arms while still delivering functional data.\" Second: \"Leaving the other five groups (eionet_cdr, infrasound, fire radiation, TEC/pseudoranges, vis_nmi/morph_sigma, FDSN BHZ) unaddressed means they will remain broken and could cause downstream errors.\" Riss: \"Six residual groups still lack Quantity-/Channel-Arms (e.g., FDSN BHZ identity), so the system will have incomplete coverage despite the parser fix.\"\n\nMake sure each line matches format exactly.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"We need to answer three questions, each in format:\n\n`R-<x> Verdikt: <A|B|C|D> — Begründung: <two sentences> — Riss: <strongest counter-evidence or unmeasured size>`\n\nWe need to choose one of the options for each. Provide a verdict (A/B/C/D) and a brief justification (two sentences) and a \"Riss\" (counter-evidence or unmeasured size) field.\n\nWe must not invent facts. Use given info. Let's analyze each.\n\n### R-b: GRS80/gamma0 registry\n\nProblem: phi/sources.phi missing arm for scalar reference constants; a, 1/f, GM, omega, gamma_e, gamma_p measured but not registerable. N = T/gamma0 in src/archivar/gfc.rs:404 remains None. calc.js is local-only (no license notice); GeographicLib is MIT code, not dataset.\n\nO