ts under 2 GiB, and is release-worthy. It also likely has epoch defined? Not sure. The abstract says 5399 but file says 5480; epoch not occupied. However, the compiler refuses without --epoch, so we need epoch set. If we choose D=2190, we still need epoch. But maybe we can set epoch via static compiler path? The question asks to choose one option. Probably A is best because it's the official partial model, smaller, release-worthy. The other options are larger or not official. So verdict A.\n\nJustification: two sentences. Riss: counter-evidence: epoch not set, compiler refuses; also abstract vs file discrepancy. So Riss could be \"epoch not occupied, compiler error\". Or \"size 2190 MB still > 2 GiB? Actually 999 MB < 2 GiB, okay.\n\n### R-g: P10 residuals\n\nProblem: six residual groups have name and unit but no matching Quantity-/Channel-Arm: eionet_cdr_* (276, kg, tau=1a), Infrasound signal sizes, Fire radiation power/bandpowers, TEC/Pseudoranges/Delay, vis_nmi/morph_sigma, Stellar metadata (Teff/logg/mag), FDSN BHZ channel identity, kg/(m^2 s)-token (parser splits on whitespace).\n\nOptions:\nA build all arms (largest architectural act).\nB smallest safe subset (kg/(m^2 s)-parser fix + stellar metadata axis).\nC build nothing, let cracks fall.\nD one form per residual.\n\nAdditional: Does parser fix + stellar axis suffice, or is FDSN key splitting also minimally needed?\n\nWe need to decide. The smallest safe subset likely B, focusing on parser fix for kg/(m^2 s) token and stellar metadata axis. That addresses the most critical parsing issue. The other groups are less essential. So verdict B.\n\nJustification: two sentences. Riss: strongest counter-evidence: missing FDSN BHZ channel identity and other residual groups still broken, leading to incomplete coverage. Or \"six residual groups still lack Quantity-/Channel-Arms\". Provide that.\n\nNow format each answer:\n\n`R-b Verdikt: A — Begründung: ... — Riss: ...`\n\nMake sure exactly format: `R-<x> Verdikt: <A|B|C|D> — Begründung: <two sentences> — Riss: <strongest counter-evidence or unmeasured size>`\n\nWe need three separate answers, each with its own R-x. Probably each on separate lines.\n\nLet's craft.\n\nR-b: Verdict A. Begründung: two sentences: \"Adding parser arms for ellipsoid and normal_gravity provides the missing scalar reference constants, enabling registration of a, 1/f, GM, omega, gamma0, etc. This follows the existing pattern used by River and Mountain builds, keeping changes consistent.\" Second sentence: \"Without these arms, N = T/gamma0 stays None, preventing the GRS80/gamma0 registry from being usable.\" Riss: \"N remains None (unmeasured gamma0) and calc.js stays local‑only, so the registry cannot be fully populated.\"\n\nR-f: Verdict A. Begründung: two sentences: \"D=2190 (XGM2019e_2159) is the official partial model, fits under the 2 GiB release threshold, and avoids the 5.95 GiB full dump that is not release‑worthy. It also reduces storage and streaming overhead while preserving the core model data.\" Second: \"The epoch is still missing, causing the compiler to reject builds without --epoch, so a separate epoch handling step is required before the block can be used.\" Riss: \"Epoch not occupied in the file, compiler error without --epoch, and abstract/file size mismatch (5399 vs 5480) create uncertainty.\"\n\nR-g: Verdict B. Begründung: two sentences: \"Fixing the kg/(m^2 s) token parser and adding a stellar metadata axis resolves the most critical parsing failures and restores usability for the majority of residual groups. This minimal change avoids the massive architectural effort of building all arms while still delivering functional data.\" Second: \"Leaving the other five groups (eionet_cdr, infrasound, fire radiation, TEC/pseudoranges, vis_nmi/morph_sigma, FDSN BHZ) unaddressed means they will remain broken and could cause downstream errors.\" Riss: \"Six residual groups still lack Quantity-/Channel-Arms (e.g., FDSN BHZ identity), so the system will have incomplete coverage despite the parser fix.\"\n\nMake sure each line matches format exactly.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":743,"completion_tokens":2157,"total_tokens":2900,"cost":0,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1712,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}